Let x y z t : Prop. Assume (x -> z) /\ (y -> t) (h1) and x /\ y (h2). We prove z /\ t.

- Going back to the definition of and (match) in h1, we prove z /\ t:
  - Assume x -> z (i) and y -> t (j). Going back to the definition of and (match) in h2, we prove z /\ t:
    - Assume x (k) and y (l).
      - Applying i to k, we have z.
      - Applying j to l, we have t.

      So by definition of and (conj), we have z /\ t.

