Let x y z t : Prop. Assume (x -> z) /\ (y -> t) (H). We prove x /\ y -> z /\ t.

- Going back to the definition of and (match) in H, we prove x /\ y -> z /\ t:
  - Assume x -> z (Hxz), y -> t (Hyt) and x /\ y (H0). Going back to the definition of and (match) in H0, we prove z /\ t:
    - Assume x (Hx) and y (Hy).
      - Applying Hxz to Hx, we have z.
      - Prove t.

      So by definition of and (conj), we have z /\ t.

